      "content": "*Clostridium perfringens* is a spore-forming bacterium that thrives in the temperature range between $40^{\\circ}\\text{F}$ and $140^{\\circ}\\text{F}$ (the danger zone). During slow cooling, this temperature range persists for too long, allowing the dormant spores to germinate into vegetative cells. These active cells then multiply rapidly, producing toxins that can cause significant foodborne illness even if the food reaches a safe final temperature.",
